sequenceDiagram
    participant Client as External Client
    participant GW as Kuadrant/Authorino<br/>Gateway
    participant API as API Server<br/>8000/TCP HTTP/HTTPS
    participant PG as PostgreSQL<br/>5432/TCP
    participant Redis as Redis/Valkey<br/>6379/TCP
    participant S3 as S3 Storage<br/>443/TCP HTTPS
    participant Proc as Processor
    participant Router as llm-d Router<br/>HTTP/HTTPS
    participant Async as llm-d-async<br/>Redis Queues
    participant GC as Garbage Collector

    Note over Client,S3: Flow 1: Batch Job Submission

    Client->>GW: POST /v1/files<br/>Auth: API key / SA token
    GW->>API: Forward + X-MaaS-Username header
    API->>S3: Upload input file (JSONL)<br/>TLS 1.2+, AWS IAM
    S3-->>API: Upload confirmed
    API->>PG: Store file metadata<br/>TLS, conn string auth
    API->>Redis: Store file status<br/>TLS optional
    API-->>GW: 200 OK (file_id)
    GW-->>Client: File uploaded

    Client->>GW: POST /v1/batches<br/>{input_file_id, model, endpoint}
    GW->>API: Forward + X-MaaS-Username header
    API->>PG: Create batch record (CAS)<br/>TLS, conn string auth
    API->>Redis: Enqueue to priority queue (ZSET)<br/>Publish batch event (stream)
    API-->>GW: 200 OK (batch_id, status: validating)
    GW-->>Client: Batch created

    Note over Proc,S3: Flow 2: Batch Job Processing (Sync Mode)

    loop Poll queue
        Proc->>Redis: ZPOPMIN from priority queue
    end
    Redis-->>Proc: Job dequeued
    Proc->>S3: Download input file<br/>TLS 1.2+, AWS IAM
    S3-->>Proc: JSONL file content
    Proc->>PG: Update status → in_progress

    loop For each request in batch (up to 50K)
        Proc->>Router: POST /v1/chat/completions<br/>TLS 1.2+ + mTLS optional<br/>Bearer token optional
        Note over Proc,Router: AIMD concurrency control:<br/>backoff on 429/5xx
        Router-->>Proc: Inference response
    end

    Proc->>S3: Upload output file<br/>TLS 1.2+, AWS IAM
    Proc->>S3: Upload error file (if any)
    Proc->>PG: Update status → completed<br/>Store output_file_id
    Proc->>Redis: Publish completion event

    Note over Proc,Async: Flow 3: Batch Job Processing (Async Mode)

    Proc->>Redis: ZPOPMIN from priority queue
    Proc->>S3: Download input file
    loop For each request in batch
        Proc->>Async: Submit to async request queue<br/>Redis 6379/TCP
    end
    loop Poll for results
        Proc->>Async: Poll result queue<br/>Redis 6379/TCP
        Async-->>Proc: Inference results
    end
    Proc->>S3: Upload output file
    Proc->>PG: Update status → completed

    Note over GC,S3: Flow 4: Garbage Collection & Reconciliation

    loop Periodic scan
        GC->>PG: Query expired batches/files
        PG-->>GC: Expired records
        GC->>S3: Delete expired files<br/>TLS 1.2+
        GC->>Redis: Remove status/event keys
        GC->>PG: Delete metadata records
    end

    loop Reconciliation scan
        GC->>Redis: Check in-flight entries<br/>(stale heartbeats)
        Redis-->>GC: Orphaned jobs
        GC->>Redis: Re-enqueue orphaned jobs<br/>to priority queue
        GC->>PG: Reset job status → pending
    end

    Note over Client,GC: Client can check status anytime
    Client->>GW: GET /v1/batches/{batch_id}
    GW->>API: Forward + tenant header
    API->>PG: Query batch record
    API->>Redis: Get real-time progress counters
    API-->>GW: Batch status + progress
    GW-->>Client: Status response
